## 🟠 HIGH PRIORITY — Core Feature Gaps

### 4. Stripe Checkout integration
- Currently `handleSubscribe` opens a WhatsApp link with a pre-filled message.
- Implement actual Stripe Checkout Sessions or Stripe Customer Portal for self-serve billing. The `stripe` package is already installed.

### 5. Email account setup UX
- The email page has a settings modal for adding IMAP/SMTP accounts but it's deeply buried.
- Show a prominent "Connect your first email account" CTA when no accounts exist, similar to how the credentials page works for WhatsApp.

### 6. Operative Versioning & Rollback
- Allow users to save snapshots of operative configurations (prompt, tone, language) and roll back to a previous version if a change doesn't perform well.
- Store version history per operative with timestamps and diff view.

### 7. Knowledge Base Versioning
- Track changes to training data over time. Allow users to view what was added/removed and revert to a previous knowledge state.
- Useful for auditing why an operative's behavior changed.

### 8. Bulk Training Data Import
- Support importing multiple files at once (drag-and-drop batch upload).
- Add CSV/JSON bulk import for structured data (e.g., FAQ lists from spreadsheets).

### 9. Operative Analytics Dashboard
- Track per-operative metrics: messages handled, average response time, resolution rate, knowledge chunk hit rate.
- Show a weekly/monthly trend graph per operative to help users understand performance.

### 10. Conversation Analytics
- Aggregate conversation data: busiest hours, common topics, customer satisfaction signals.
- Export conversation summaries for reporting.

