## 🟡 MEDIUM PRIORITY — Power Features

### 11. Operative Prompt Templates
- Pre-built prompt templates for common use cases (appointment booking, lead qualification, FAQ handling, complaint resolution).
- Users can browse templates and customize before deploying.

### 12. Scheduled Training Runs
- Allow users to schedule recurring knowledge syncs (e.g., re-crawl a website weekly to pick up new articles).
- Show a schedule UI with next-run countdown.

### 13. Knowledge Freshness Detection
- Automatically flag training data that hasn't been updated in X days.
- Show a "stale" indicator on old chunks and suggest re-ingestion.

### 14. Multi-Channel Message Routing Rules
- Let users define routing rules: e.g., "If message contains 'billing', route to billing operative; otherwise route to general support."
- Visual rule builder in the dashboard.

### 15. Operative A/B Testing
- Deploy two versions of an operative to different traffic splits and compare performance metrics.
- Auto-select the winner after a configurable test period.

### 16. Audit Log
- Track all system changes: who deployed/modified which operative, when training data was added/removed, billing events.
- Filterable log view in the dashboard.

### 17. API Key Management
- Let users generate API keys for programmatic access to their operatives.
- Show key usage stats, allow revocation, and rate limiting configuration.

### 18. Webhook Configuration
- Allow users to set up outgoing webhooks for events (new message, operative error, billing event).
- Webhook management UI with test-send functionality.

### 19. Operative Marketplace
- Let users publish their operative templates to a public marketplace.
- Other users can browse, clone, and customize published templates.

